      "bbox": {
        "l": 94.7339,
        "t": 738.0270068359374,
        "r": 244.12429999999995,
        "b": 727.2077469606776
      },
      "content": "OIL AND FILTER CHANGE",
      "level": 2,
      "role": "section"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0546",
      "reading_order": 576,
      "section": "OIL AND FILTER CHANGE",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.5654,
        "t": 715.5956068359375,
        "r": 291.47389999999996,
        "b": 667.7531492035388
      },
      "content": "Change the oil and filter at the intervals listed in Table 8-1.  Use oil that meets the API classification and SAE viscosity grade indicated in the previous section."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0547",
      "reading_order": 577,
      "section": "Engine Oil Change",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.5654,
        "t": 654.8585068359374,
        "r": 154.61739999999995,
        "b": 644.0392469606776
      },
      "content": "Engine Oil Change",
      "level": 2,
      "role": "section"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0548",
      "reading_order": 578,
      "section": "Engine Oil Change",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.56539999999999,
        "t": 632.4271068359375,
        "r": 291.6818000000006,
        "b": 584.5846492035388
      },
      "content": "Run the engine until thoroughly warm.  Stop the engine, open the drain valve (Figure 8-1) and drain the oil into a container.  When completely drained, close the valve and refill the crankcase with new oil."
    },
    {
      "type": "admonition",
      "id": "txt_0549",
      "reading_order": 579,
      "section": "Engine Oil Change",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.565599999999996,
        "t": 570.5751068359375,
        "r": 291.6149000000001,
        "b": 522.6733519502826
      },
      "content": "WARNING Hot crankcase oil can cause burns if it is spilled or splashed on skin.  Keep fingers and hands clear when removing the oil drain plug and wear protective clothing.",
      "severity": "warning"
    },
    {
      "type": "admonition",
      "id": "txt_0550",
      "reading_order": 580,
      "section": "Engine Oil Change",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.565599999999996,
        "t": 508.7232068359375,
        "r": 291.4037000000001,
        "b": 486.16325195028264
      },
      "content": "WARNING State or federal agencies have determined that prolonged contact with used engine oil can cause cancer or reproductive toxicity.    When  adding,  changing  or  working  with used  oil,  take  care  not  to  breathe,  ingest  or come into  excessive  contact  with  these  substances.  Wash hands after use.  Wear protective clothing and equipment.  Provide adequate ventilation.",
      "severity": "warning"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0551",
      "reading_order": 581,
      "section": "Oil Filter Change",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9386,
        "t": 638.7010068359375,
        "r": 417.2626000000004,
        "b": 627.8817469606777
      },
      "content": "Oil Filter Change",
      "level": 2,
      "role": "section"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0552",
      "reading_order": 582,
      "section": "Oil Filter Change",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9386,
        "t": 615.7594068359375,
        "r": 564.9890000000007,
        "b": 555.2746492035388
      },
      "content": "Spin off the oil filter and discard it.  Thoroughly clean the filter mounting surface.  Apply a thin film of oil to the filter gasket, and spin the filter on until the gasket just touches the mounting pad.  Then turn an additional 3/4 turn.  Do not over-tighten the filter."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0553",
      "reading_order": 583,
      "section": "Oil Filter Change",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9386,
        "t": 541.7756068359377,
        "r": 564.9526999999997,
        "b": 506.57544920353894
      },
      "content": "With oil in the crankcase, start the set and check for leakage around the filter gasket.  Tighten the filter only enough to eliminate leaks."
    },
